    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a volatile slate today, with our primary value driven by **Sam Antonacci** and **Nasim Nunez**. **Sam Antonacci** headlines our daily efficiency scores at 63.61; his premier placement in the leadoff spot against Kumar Rocker, combined with a favorable platoon advantage, positions him as our most reliable engine for runs. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** provides the most interesting upside at a 61.73 score. Despite an assumed #8 spot in the order, his efficiency is buoyed significantly by the weak 5.10 xERA of Ryan Feltner, making him a sneaky play to capitalize on lower-leverage situations. While **Jackson Merrill** (51.66) faces a tougher test against Braxton Ashcraft\u2019s 3.28 xERA, his dynamic platoon advantage remains high, keeping him in the lineup despite a slight dip in base projection.\n\nOur middle-tier options, **Miguel Vargas** (55.00) and **Liam Hicks** (47.26), face the tall task of navigating a tough matchup against Kumar Rocker and Framber Valdez, respectively. **Miguel Vargas** earns a start primarily due to his solid xwOBA of 0.389, which helps mitigate the threat posed by Rocker. Conversely, **Liam Hicks** sits at the bottom of our start threshold; his score is hampered by a significant negative platoon adjustment against the left-handed Framber Valdez. We are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, as any shift from our assumed batting orders\u2014particularly for **Sam Antonacci** or **Miguel Vargas**\u2014could force a late-afternoon reevaluation. With core studs like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** inactive due to team off-days, our bench remains thin today, leaving **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to provide depth should weather alerts or late lineup scratches materialize.",
